Let build.rs consume a pre-generated src_binding.rs.

Bindgen's top-level run over V8's vendored libc++ needs a Clang 19+
libclang. When none is available the binding cannot be produced locally,
so allow an externally supplied, content-addressed one to stand in.

The build recipe verifies that file against the component manifest's
hashes.rust_binding and runtime.rusty_v8_revision before exporting
V8_PREBUILT_BINDING, so this branch never widens what the build trusts.

This diff deliberately carries ONE hunk. It used to also carry the
`target_os == "android"` sysroot hunk that 0002-install-sysroot.patch
already applies; that made the two patches collide (patch --forward
refuses an already-applied hunk) and, worse, forced any sentinel taken
from the last hunk to be 0002's sentinel, which is present before this
patch runs and would therefore report it as applied when it is not.

diff --git a/build.rs b/build.rs
index 970e88b..a968545 100644
--- a/build.rs
+++ b/build.rs
@@ -141,6 +141,26 @@ fn acquire_lock() -> LockFile {
 }

 fn build_binding() {
+  // MIGO: allow reusing a pre-generated src_binding.rs (same bindgen
+  // 0.72 + same V8 14.5.201 = identical FFI ABI) to skip the local
+  // bindgen step, which would otherwise require a Clang 19+ libclang to
+  // parse V8's vendored libc++ headers. Set V8_PREBUILT_BINDING to the
+  // path of a known-good src_binding.rs.
+  if let Ok(prebuilt) = env::var("V8_PREBUILT_BINDING") {
+    if Path::new(&prebuilt).is_file() {
+      let out_path = build_dir().join("gn_out").join("src_binding.rs");
+      fs::copy(&prebuilt, &out_path)
+        .expect("MIGO: failed to copy V8_PREBUILT_BINDING");
+      println!(
+        "cargo:rustc-env=RUSTY_V8_SRC_BINDING_PATH={}",
+        out_path.display()
+      );
+      println!("cargo:warning=MIGO: using prebuilt binding {prebuilt}");
+      return;
+    }
+    panic!("V8_PREBUILT_BINDING set but not a file: {prebuilt}");
+  }
+
   // Bindgen needs Clang 19+ for V8's libc++ builtin type traits.
   if env::var("LIBCLANG_PATH").is_err() {
     eprintln!("Warning: LIBCLANG_PATH not set. Bindgen requires Clang 19+.");
